WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:09.110
- Only thing it is,
man, I had a rough life.

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:10.780
I lived in the neighborhood where

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:15.343
there was no pity for the weak.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.313
You couldn't smile at 'em,
you didn't have no sympathy,

00:00:18.313 --> 00:00:20.390
you didn't have no remorse.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:23.310
If he got in the way, and
he did the wrong thing,

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:26.380
you broke his ass off and
you left him where he at.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.550
Ain't no going back to
clean him up, you know?

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.230
If he bleeding and shit, you know?

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:34.310
I had a homie that was
kickin' it with me over here

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:37.170
in the neighborhood, and he hit the dude

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.020
in the face with a bottle.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.000
And, man, do you know what it feels like

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.514
to get hit in the face
with a glass, glass bottle?

00:00:44.514 --> 00:00:45.840
And then the skin just tear?

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:50.793
And you lookin' at him
like, what do you do?

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.200
And these motherfuckers right here,

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.290
I gotta roll with them,
because if I don't roll

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:58.120
with them, I'ma be one of them dudes

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.800
gettin' hit with the fucking bottle, too.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.950
So, I don't want that, I'd
rather just say fuck it,

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.450
I'm riding with y'all.

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:07.842
Shit, peer pressure is a mug, you know?

00:01:07.842 --> 00:01:10.092
And when you don't have
nobody with you, dog,

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.170
that's just the way it is, you know?

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:17.620
I mean, I coulda asked the homie,

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:19.183
dog, why you doin' some shit like that?

00:01:19.183 --> 00:01:22.440
That nigga probably woulda
jumped in my ass, man.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:24.100
So, I ain't trippin'.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.390
But you got people that,

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:29.560
I got some little homies, man,

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.100
they did a little drive by, right?

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.660
I'm sitting in the county jail,

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:35.280
I'm in here for robbery right now,

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.013
and he come in for a drive by.

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:40.860
I said, dog, what happened?

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:44.007
He said, "Man, we went over one, dog,

00:01:44.007 --> 00:01:45.467
"we went and did our thing".

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.440
I say, nigga, I heard
you was drunk, nigga,

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:50.640
and the police chased y'all,

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.190
and y'all ran the car
up a pole or something

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:54.240
Nigga, what happened?

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:59.177
He said, "Hey, dog, we
busted on these niggas,

00:01:59.177 --> 00:02:02.237
"and the police were
comin' around the corner

00:02:02.237 --> 00:02:05.587
"as we was bustin', and that's how they

00:02:05.587 --> 00:02:07.522
"got up on us and stuff.

00:02:07.522 --> 00:02:09.687
"And so I tried to punch it and shit,

00:02:09.687 --> 00:02:10.827
"and I tried to punch it all the way

00:02:10.827 --> 00:02:13.417
"back to the hood and stuff, and I ran."

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:19.223
I said, man, so, did you shoot the dude?

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:22.293
You know where he shot the dude at?

00:02:22.293 --> 00:02:25.043
He shot the dude in the damn leg.

00:02:26.013 --> 00:02:27.410
Do you get recognition for that?

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:29.523
Do you pat a nigga on the back for that?

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:33.727
They was like, "Damn, dog,
where'd you shoot him at?"

00:02:33.727 --> 00:02:35.217
"I shot him in the leg."

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.077
You know, "What kind of gun you had?"

00:02:39.077 --> 00:02:40.740
"A .380."

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:45.740
You had a small gun,
small bullets, small car.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:52.670
Not enough gas to get
away from them one time,

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:53.793
so you got caught.

00:02:56.735 --> 00:02:58.320
So, is the dude coming to court?

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.193
Hell, yeah, he comin' to
court to testify against him.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.420
And make it so cold,
you believe me or not,

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:08.810
usually when you shot a
person above the waist

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.310
is when you really get some time.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:16.020
They gave my little homie life

00:03:16.976 --> 00:03:19.453
for shootin' that motherfucker in the leg.

00:03:19.453 --> 00:03:22.230
I'da got my motherfuckin' ass
out of that motherfuckin' car,

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:25.120
walked up, and knocked that nigga down.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:28.033
That's how you, if you're
gonna go do some dumb shit.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:30.860
You know, but somewhere along the line,

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:33.600
somebody gotta be the smart man

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:38.313
and wake up and recognize reality
and know what's real, man.

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:42.680
I got another homie, let me tell you,

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:46.330
that thought they was goin'
up, goin' to do a drive-by,

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.670
and they went in this apartment building

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:51.610
and threw a bunch of
bombs in these apartments,

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:53.113
and blew up kids.

00:03:54.943 --> 00:03:56.800
And instead of them
gettin' the death penalty,

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:01.443
they took the life without,
with no possibility of parole.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.850
So, the neighborhood I come from,

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:09.753
it's always been a tough
neighborhood to live in.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:13.490
And it's just not the neighborhood itself,

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:14.363
it's the peoples.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.940
'Cause the neighborhood don't make it bad,

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.540
it's the peoples that's
there that make it bad.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:26.137
And, Hell, I done been
placed in positions where,

00:04:26.137 --> 00:04:27.417
"Man, go get the gun, dog.

00:04:27.417 --> 00:04:28.270
"We fi'n' to go do somethin'."

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:31.147
And if I, man, I don't
wanna roll with that,

00:04:31.147 --> 00:04:34.785
"Nigga, what you mean you don't
wanna roll with that, nigga?

00:04:34.785 --> 00:04:36.135
"Nigga, you rollin', nigga!

00:04:37.187 --> 00:04:39.137
"You ain't down with us in this stuff?"

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:40.940
No, man.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:43.203
What, you tell a motherfucka I'm sick?

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.443
I got the flu, man, I can't go right now.

00:04:47.297 --> 00:04:50.497
"Nigga, you better get
your ass on out here, man.

00:04:50.497 --> 00:04:51.330
"Come on."

00:04:52.219 --> 00:04:55.370
All right, dog, I got you,
I got you, I'm comin'.

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:59.000
So, when you up against shit like that,

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.410
and peoples that ain't been up in,

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:03.230
a lot of these dudes
down here you see now,

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:07.513
they come from nice homes,
nice family, good background,

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:12.540
firm education that help
'em get certain things

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:15.380
that they needed in order
to go to the next step

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:18.430
of college or whatever, you know?

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:19.930
I didn't get that chance, dog.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:26.103
Because we didn't have
enough to push ahead.

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:30.200
Maybe I shoulda been smart
enough when I got a little older.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.780
But I was already incarcerated,

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:35.540
and I was already
adapted to the negativity

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:39.613
that makes you a bad person in society.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:46.180
I don't wanna call myself
any bad person now,

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:51.150
because I think that
everybody deserves a chance

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.653
to see what's real and what's not real.

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:57.750
And, if I can go back and
turn the hands of time,

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.330
I would do the right thing.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:02.290
Because I know it's a lot
more opportunities out there,

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:04.900
and a lot more things
that coulda happened,

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:08.890
that could have been in my
favor where I coulda did better,

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:11.443
and where I coulda had my own home,

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:14.810
maybe even a little small business.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:17.490
I don't know, but I coulda had a lot more

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:22.740
laid in my position if
I'da took the time out,

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:25.560
stayed in school, and
listened to my mother.

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:28.750
But, some of the bad things that I learned

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:32.133
was pushed from my mother,
because she was, like,

00:06:33.427 --> 00:06:34.947
"Why you hangin' around these little boys?

00:06:34.947 --> 00:06:38.570
"Why don't you go around with
some peoples older your age?"

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:43.010
I told her that, shit,
the niggas that's my age,

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:46.782
they gangs and stuff,
they were with gangs.

00:06:46.782 --> 00:06:51.087
And so she was, like,
"Well, why don't you hang

00:06:51.087 --> 00:06:53.400
"with Eric and Michael now?"

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.040
Shit, I did.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.570
When we went to school,
we was at the school,

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:59.820
and them niggas left, and
niggas come up to school

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:00.830
and take our shit.

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:03.880
I ain't gonna be with
no niggas that's scared.

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:05.250
I wanna be with somebody that ain't

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.953
gonna take nobody's bullshit.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:11.990
So, that's why I made the
decisions the way I made 'em.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:16.990
It was wrong, and I couldn't
show it in my mother's eyes

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.870
because she only wanted
the best things for me.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:24.870
But she didn't know
what I had to deal with

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.113
when it was time to go to school,

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.410
when it was time to walk the streets,

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.973
when it was time to hang out.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:35.430
She didn't know nothin' about that,

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:38.630
'cause she was too busy
sittin' in the house, drinkin',

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:39.903
or doin' her own thing.

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:45.253
So, I made my decisions for myself.

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:50.090
And I had three younger brothers
that was younger than me

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:53.600
that I needed to show support to.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:55.340
So, if they had problems,

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:58.143
I wanted to let them know to come get me,

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:01.290
and I'll stand up for you, dog.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:02.313
I'll fight for you.

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:06.960
And I remember my little
brother, plain as day,

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:09.600
he had a problem one day with a dude,

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:11.597
and he come get me, sayin', "Hey, SB,

00:08:11.597 --> 00:08:13.880
"this nigga over here
trippin' on me and stuff."

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:15.680
And I said, I got you.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:16.940
Come on, let's go right here,

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:18.470
let this nigga know right now, nigga,

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:21.800
not to, you know, mess
with you anymore, nigga.

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:23.000
And I went around there,

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:26.440
and he came and got his brothers,

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:28.680
he went and got his brothers
to do it up for the fight.

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:30.523
And I went and got my brothers,

00:08:31.582 --> 00:08:35.250
and I told him, look, however we do it,

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:37.170
it's still gonna be cool.

00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:39.150
I knocked that nigga out.

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:41.330
My little brother, he was happy.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:45.690
But it made us move, now, to where

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:48.543
we thought we was hardcores now, you know?

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:55.220
I mean, thinkin' again,
I just wanna say, man,

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:02.213
after seein' all the things I did in life,

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:05.096
I would want somethin' better than

00:09:05.096 --> 00:09:08.630
what I lived on that stage right there.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:10.230
'Cause it didn't get me nothin'.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:13.617
Now, I'm up in age, and I have nothin'.

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:17.340
I'm just tryin' to be peaceful now.

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:21.030
I still carry the gang
activities when it's necessary,

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:22.673
and I'm a gang affiliated.

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:27.970
Because I come from an area
where that's all I knew.

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:29.230
That's all I know.

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:30.760
That's all I stand by.

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:32.493
That's all I'll take to my grave.

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:34.620
It is what it is.

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:37.350
I won't count the number,
I just roll with it.

